    {
      "name": "Independent Segments",
      "type": "trait",
      "_id": "gNCAI3Ao3pxTnHyf",
      "img": "modules/impmal-core/assets/icons/blank.webp",
      "system": {
        "notes": {
         "player": "",
          "gm": "<p>Once inside a victim, the boreworm starts to break apart, with each segment becoming a new boreworm roughly once every hour (an average worm has 8-12 segments), which start eating on its own after five minutes. Each segment comes with Burrowing Teeth and causes damage on its own. Victims are usually dead by the time new boreworms are large enough to split into segments themselves. Removing these boreworms can be done with a successful Hard (-10) Medicae (Human) Test, which takes one hour.</p>"
        },
